19.text:
PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Core facts remain undisputed: Lyz:HaloTag-eGFP (neutrophils) + mpeg1:SNAPtag-DsRed (macrophages); chloroalkane-Cy5 probe covalently labels only HaloTag after 48 hpf pulse/wash, adding ~630 nm signal exclusively to neutrophils alongside constitutive eGFP (488 nm). No SNAP ligand supplied, so DsRed stays unlabeled. Tail-fin injury triggers neutrophil-first recruitment (minutes–hours), so earliest post-injury signals arise from the two neutrophil channels only.  

Round-1 shift: strong consensus now on D (Colleagues 1,3,4,6,8,10–12,15,18–20), with prior G advocates (e.g., 2,5,7,9,13,14,16,17,21) largely conceding the temporal reading of “first” and lack of evidence for meaningful residual-dye/SNAP cross-reactivity/AF bleed under the stated wash+dark-growth protocol. Minority G hold-outs still cite 1 µM/2 h pulse + single wash + 2-day incubation as possible sources of 559 nm crosstalk or injury AF, but these are now explicitly challenged as unsupported speculation.  

Preserved disagreements: (1) strict temporal (“first after wounding”) vs. “any active fluorophore” reading of the question; (2) practical wash efficiency and filter-set bleed for the long-chain Cy5 analog. No support for SNAP cross-reactivity or major wash failure. Temporal-recruitment argument remains dominant and consistent with zebrafish immunology. Unresolved: exact quantitative residual-dye levels, but protocol details favor clean D. My view unchanged—D is correct.}

